    "created_at": "2026-01-20T01:01:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-25T07:27:04Z",
    "body": "> I'm not really sure I understand your suggestion about tracking elements instead.\n\nThis was mostly to avoid keeping an arbitrarily growing set of documents (even if weak), though if the scoped document set can indeed be weak then this can implemented as an unobservable optimization anyway.\n\nEssentially by changing it to elements, it would've looked something like this in `define`:\n\n```diff\n- for (const document of this.#scopedDocumentSet) {\n-     this.#upgradeRelevantElements(document);\n- }\n+ const scopedDocuments = new Set<Document>();\n+ for (const element of this.#elementsToUpgrade) {\n+    if (element.isConnected) {\n+         scopedDocuments.add(element.ownerDocument);\n+    }\n+    // don't need to track this element once it's document is scheduled for upgrading\n+    this.#elementsToUpgrade.delete(element);\n+ }\n+ // Alternatively to this loop, this.#elementsToUpgrade could just be sorted by tree order\n+ for (const document of scopedDocuments) {\n+     this.#upgradeRelevantElements(document);\n+ }\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
